   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to licensing\nrestrictions for manufacturers and wholesalers of alcoholic beverages on\nlicensees who sell at retail for on-premises consumption; and to repeal\ncertain provisions of such law relating thereto; and providing for the repeal\nof certain provisions upon the expiration thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S8737",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8737-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Rpld §101 sub 1 ¶ (a) sub¶ (ii), amd §§101 & 106, ABC L",
    "lawSection": "Alcoholic Beverage Control Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8737\n\nSPONSOR: HELMING\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to\nlicensing restrictions for manufacturers and wholesalers of alcoholic\nbeverages on licensees who sell at retail for on-premises consumption;\nand to repeal certain provisions of such law relating thereto; and\nproviding for the repeal of certain provisions upon the expiration ther-\neof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo make technical corrections and remedies of metes and bounds to\ncontinue the operation of a hotel in Canandaigua, NY to maintain its\nability to hold a retail liquor license for on-premise consumption and\ncontinue the approval of an exemption on restrictions on manufacturers,\nwholesalers, and retailers from sharing an interest in a liquor license.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 removes the retailer metes and bounds from section 101.a of\nABC law and inserts language of metes and bounds for the wholesaler or\nmanufacturer.\n\nSections 2 through 4 insert the retailer metes and bounds into the ABC\nlaw. Section 5 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation seeks technical amendments to the ABC law based in\norder to align the metes and bounds for the hotel on Canandaigua Lake,\nNY, that has been approved for liquor licenses, historically after\nchange of ownership and the pursuant legislative approval of the\nlicenses since 1995. While there have been two additional legislative\nactions in the past 25 years on this legislation, the technical\ncorrections had not been flagged until recently. This legislation has\nbeen introduced in order to act swiftly to continue to abide by all ABC\nlaws.\n\nThe ground-up rebuild of the former Inn on the Lake, The Lake House on\nCanandaigua Lake will be a showcase and point of pride for NYS and\nbeyond. The world-class hotel will be a tourist destination and continue\nto provide community access to the iconic Sand Bar, which is a perennial\nfavorite of locals and tourists, alike. The investment put into the\nhotel and community by the family that has owned and rebuilt the Lake\nHouse exemplifies the commitment to be an economic driver for the area.\nThere are 42 newly built public access docks along the lakefront, as\nwell as integrated programming with its neighbor, a charitable organiza-\ntion promoting New York's agricultural, food, and beverage industries.\n\nThis legislation is supported locally, and necessary in order to provide\nfor the operation of the hotel, which has a significant economic and\nlocal impact in the Canandaigua community.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
